.Dd October 21, 2026
.Dt SWITCHBOARD-NSS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm switchboard-nss
.Nd private account lookup helper for SwitchBoard
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
helper reads one bounded binary request from standard input, requires end of
input, performs an NSS account lookup, and writes one bounded binary reply to
standard output.
It supports passwd lookup by name or UID, group lookup by name,
and supplementary group membership through
.Xr getgrouplist 3 .
It does not return passwords or file descriptors.
The protocol is private to the matching system generation.
.Pp
The caller must remove inherited software authority and privileged descriptors
and prevent privilege acquisition before executing this helper.
The caller must also validate all returned data, enforce a deadline, and reap
the helper.
This program alone does not establish an isolation boundary.
SwitchBoard uses this helper for ordinary account lookups in BIP mode.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Lookup errors are returned in the reply; malformed framing and I/O failures
cause a nonzero exit status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getgrnam 3 ,
.Xr getgrouplist 3 ,
.Xr getpwnam 3 ,
.Xr getpwuid 3 ,
.Xr nsswitch.conf 5 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
